 "weaknesses": [
  "Killed job loses up to one CHUNK (200 roasters) of work: the day-5 kill at 349 done kept 200, so 149 were refetched",
  "WooCommerce outage: robots.txt 503 -> RobotsUnavailable, which PR62 does not defer, so the first slot failed all 233; recovery depends on the resume slot being after the outage (fixed 6 h here)",
  "S2 IP limit: limiter at 3 req/s trips 16 platform cooldowns and 741 IP 429s; Shopify job 33 -> 56 min. A per-connector rps (e.g. 1.8) would avoid it; the limiter recovers but halving + 0.97x speed-up oscillates",
  "raw/ compaction rewrites and deletes files: fine on GCS, but HF commits need delete operations; the lake's 'never rewrite' rule holds only outside raw/",
  "A week's data is spread over 5 days of fetched_at under one run_date; price changes between Mon and Fri land in the same week",
  "11 schedule entries instead of 1; a connector job that silently never runs is caught only at merge",
  "S2 (IP-wide limit) got worse with v2: backed-off stores are 'quiet hosts', so their 429s never trip the platform pause. The first Shopify job parked 433 and the end-of-week Shopify ok fell to 86.7% (v0: 93.1%). Quiet hosts should still count when many distinct stores block together",
  "Refusers cost 3 backoffs (7 min) in each Shopify job and its resume; they could skip to crawl-retry once refused this week",
  "The conditional short-page stop needs history: on a fresh lake (the real run) every store still asks for the empty page",
  "registry.current classifies the last ok batch in Python on every call (one duckdb read of snapshots + bodies)"
 ],
